# {{id}}

A cox plugin scaffolded by `cox plugin new {{id}} --lang go`. `docs/design/plugins.md`
(PL) and `docs/plugins.md` in the [cox repository](https://github.com/pyrlyn/cox)
have the full contract; this file only covers this package.

Capabilities asked for at scaffold time: {{with_summary}}. Edit `plugin.toml`'s
`[capabilities]` to change them, and `main.go` for the exports that back them.

## Build

```
mise use go tinygo   # once, or install Go and TinyGo yourself
just build
```

builds `{{crate_name}}.wasm` with TinyGo (`-target wasip1 -buildmode=c-shared`).
`plugin.toml` has `wasi = true` because TinyGo's runtime imports WASI.

## Try it

```
just smoke
```

builds the module and runs `smoke_test.go`, which installs the package into a
scratch `COX_HOME` with `cox plugin install --yes` and checks that
`cox plugin list --json` reports it `loaded`. `cox` must be on `PATH`.

## Install for real

```
cox plugin install . --yes
```
